sweet ufs: recover a stalled command, and publish the poll counter

bp19 served 1.09 GB through the direct DMA path and then stopped on a
56 block read: the UFS lock stayed with one thread for 84 minutes with
"age 5049 s ... err 0 x0", so the completion wait (which has a 5 s
deadline) is not where it sits - either the register read or the sleep
never returns, or the controller never completes and nothing notices.

Count the turns of the completion poll (pi in the heartbeat): a growing
count means the controller is not completing, a frozen one means the
thread is inside the register read or the block.  On timeout, clear the
doorbell and re-arm the request list instead of leaving the slot latched,
so the next command can go through and the boot can report an I/O error
instead of sitting there forever.  Also drop stale cache lines after a
direct transfer (the destination is the caller's memory now), and publish
the strategy breadcrumbs only under the lock, since a waiter was
overwriting the stuck holder's values.
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
@@ -148,6 +148,8 @@
